.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt MIXER 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mixer
.Nd the master volume, as OSS's mixer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/soundcard.h
.Pp
.Pa /dev/mixer
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The device reads and sets the master volume of the audio driver in use,
Intel HD Audio or the Sound Blaster 16, through OSS's ioctls with Linux's
numbers: major 14, minor 0.
It is there only while one of those two drivers is; the PC speaker has no
volume.
The node is mode 0666, so that the console's user sets the volume.
.Pp
The mixer has one channel, the volume, which the driver applies to every
amplifier of its output path.
A level is OSS's int: the left side's percentage, 0 to 100, in the low byte
and the right's in the next.
The driver keeps the level set and applies it again each time a stream
starts, and the console's own
.Dv AUDIO_SET_VOLUME
request sets the same level.
It is 100 when the driver starts;
.Xr init 8
then sets the level kept from the last halt, power-off or reboot, if
there is one.
The device keeps no level itself, so one set and then lost to a power cut
is not kept.
A level of 0 mutes HD Audio's amplifiers.
.Bl -tag -width SOUND_MIXER_WRITE_VOLUME
.It Dv SOUND_MIXER_READ_VOLUME
The level, the same on both sides.
.It Dv SOUND_MIXER_WRITE_VOLUME
Set the level to the louder of the two sides, and give back the level set.
.It Dv SOUND_MIXER_READ_DEVMASK
.Dv SOUND_MASK_VOLUME
alone.
.It Dv SOUND_MIXER_READ_RECMASK , SOUND_MIXER_READ_RECSRC
0: the mixer records nothing.
.It Dv SOUND_MIXER_READ_STEREODEVS , SOUND_MIXER_READ_CAPS
0: the volume is one channel.
.It Dv SOUND_MIXER_INFO
A
.Vt mixer_info :
the id,
.Dq HDA
or
.Dq SB16 ,
the driver's name, and the count of the volume's writes since boot.
.It Dv OSS_GETVERSION
0x030802, the version Linux gives.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
A read or write of another of OSS's channels, such as
.Dv SOUND_MIXER_PCM .
.It Bq Er ENOTTY
Another ioctl.
.It Bq Er ENODEV
No driver with a volume is in use.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr console 4 ,
.Xr dsp 4 ,
.Xr input 4 ,
.Xr init 8
